  "ai_language_tip": "Start in Azerbaijani (az); in Baku many businesses switch easily to Russian, which is the safest second choice; English is limited to hotels and some central Baku restaurants.",
  "english_ok": "rarely — Hotels, international restaurants and some private clinics in Baku; most shops, garages and regions speak Azerbaijani or Russian only.",
  "politeness": "Warm and respectful; formal 'Siz'; open with 'Salam' or 'Salam əleyküm'; address men as '… bəy' / 'müəllim' and women as '… xanım'; close with 'Təşəkkür edirəm, sağ olun'.",
  "name_tip": "Bookings under first name + 'bəy'/'xanım' or surname; surnames often end -ov/-ova, -li, -zadə; spell Latin names slowly — Azerbaijani uses Latin letters ə, ı, ş, ç, ğ, ö, ü.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile 0XX XXX XX XX (codes 50, 51, 55, 70, 77, 99, 10; e.g. 050 12345678), international +994; WhatsApp is the default for confirmations and locations.",
  "time_tip": "24h in writing; spoken 'saat yeddi yarım' = 7:30 but the Russian-style 'səkkizin yarısı' (half of the eighth) also = 7:30; always read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "Mobile numbers read 3-3-2-2 ('əlli, yüz iyirmi üç, qırx beş, altmış yeddi'); Russian numbers also heard in Baku.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid restaurant peaks 13:00 and 19:00–21:00, calls after 21:00, Sundays for offices, and Novruz holidays in March when much shuts for about 5 days.",
  "closed_days": "Shops and restaurants open daily; offices closed Saturday–Sunday; holidays include New Year (1–2 Jan), 20 January (mourning day), 8 March, Novruz (5 days around 20–21 March), 9 May, 28 May, 15 and 26 June, 8 and 9 November, 31 December, plus Ramazan and Gurban bayramı by lunar calendar.",
  "booking_channels": "Phone and WhatsApp dominant; Vilka and YERVAR for restaurant tables in Baku; DocFind for doctors; Wolt and Bolt Food for delivery; Bolt and Uber/local apps for taxis.",
  "voice_menu": "Azercell, Bakcell, Nar, banks and utilities use IVR; small businesses answer on a mobile directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Restaurants and clinics often confirm via WhatsApp or a call on the day; platforms send SMS.",
